<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Tens of thousands protest against far-right AfD party in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:257c5b696799c831fc3c4948b4b20c6efff5ed7b471285cdbc00751c3d06af4d</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T17:12:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-tens-of-thousands-of-people-protest-in-germany-against-far-right-afd" /><summary type="html">About 150,000 demonstrators took to the streets in around 20 cities across Germany on Saturday against the far-right AfD, after the party scored a crushing victory in a state election last week. The Alternative for Germany (AfD) topped the vote in the eastern region of Saxony-Anhalt, and is now seeking to form the first extreme-right state government in Germany since World War II.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Crocodiles pushed towards homes by rising lakes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b1463783aae8cdd8e5f1e756cc000f5f7d4fbe322a745e78aaac2550e452761</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:51:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-kenya-crocodiles-pushed-towards-homes-by-rising-lakes" /><summary type="html">Climate change is forcing Kenya's wildlife officers to go on a crocodile hunt on the shores of Lake Baringo in a bid to curb growing human-wildlife conflict. Lakes in Kenya's Rift Valley have risen to levels not seen in at least half a century, pushing the reptiles towards human homes. Officers are tasked with trapping the animals and relocating them — an operation as tricky as it is dangerous.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump in Ireland: What are Irish people saying about the visit?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6eb44358dda578f7d352af0e6d8cef8f026a0b93fee73015f5de21763bce276b</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:50:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-trump-in-ireland-what-are-irish-people-saying-about-the-visit" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump held talks Saturday in Dublin with his Irish counterpart Catherine Connolly during a weekend visit that's more about a major golf tournament hosted on a course he owns on the country's Atlantic coast. He also met with Ireland's Prime Minister Micheál Martin. We discuss that with Gavin Cooney, sports correspondent at the Irish Times.</summary></entry><entry><title>'The excitement is just too much!': Céline Dion poised for emotional comeback in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37a458d78bb7d3d2464aa0e510a1e26661d4148066db5e0e41423295b378cb34</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:49:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-the-excitement-is-just-too-much-celine-dion-poised-for-emotional-comeback-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Celine Dion was set to make her long-awaited return to the stage in Paris on Saturday after years of battling a rare neurological disorder, with anticipation among fans reaching fever pitch. "The excitement is just too much!" a fan told our journalist Jennifer Ben Brahim.</summary></entry><entry><title>French police suspect train derailment was sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:055a3a158d9c64c04bb47574683c4ae83c0cdb06a13716f2cf7c31e42719a489</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:47:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-french-police-suspect-train-derailment-was-sabotage" /><summary type="html">French investigators suspect sabotage was behind a train derailment in northwestern France that injured 44 people and left passengers in a state of shock, prosecutors said on Saturday.</summary></entry><entry><title>BRICS: What is in the joint statement from the 11 members?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c71d6417c3f6198a4bda14988574d07a7f2afcafcbdd12276a8c094f0a5a7a6</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:45:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-brics-what-is-in-the-joint-statement-from-the-11-members" /><summary type="html">Members of the 11-nation BRICS group including China, Russia, Iran and India called for calm in the Middle East at a summit in New Delhi on Saturday, overcoming earlier divisions to issue a joint statement.
 
Chinese President Xi Jinping, who joined Russian, Iranian, Indian and other leaders in India's capital, told the summit that the Middle East war "does not serve the common interests of the international community".
 
France 24's Andrew Hilliar tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>BRICS nations urge 'maximum restraint' in Middle East war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d04ead30e2fd6155c081b52d8a813c6af4c030556d701b4d993e28b5b8ee206</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T14:42:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-brics-nations-urge-maximum-restraint-in-middle-east-war" /><summary type="html">Members of the 11-nation BRICS group including China, Russia, Iran and India called for calm in the Middle East at a summit in New Delhi on Saturday, overcoming earlier divisions to issue a joint statement.</summary></entry><entry><title>Céline Dion's comeback: Why did she choose Paris?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0de50f0f6ef3674b00830c8d5c687d68712cdefcfecca41e64b2d3e2e708dff9</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T14:41:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-c%C3%A9line-dion-s-come-back-why-did-she-choose-paris" /><summary type="html">Céline Dion was set to make her long-awaited return to the stage in Paris on Saturday after years of battling a rare neurological disorder, with fans counting down the hours until showtime. But why did she choose this city? "It's not just the Olympics effect. Paris was the launch pad for her career. Beyond Quebec, through the '80s and early '90s, commentators have always mentioned that Paris is like a second home for her," says our guest Nick Rees-Roberts, professor of media, culture and communication at Sorbonne Nouvelle University.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: AfD leads in Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, Merz's CDU slumps to 7%</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05f2c2dac101243217816b068c274a3b19e19449682a32a70de347974c58c708</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T14:37:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-germany-afd-leads-in-mecklenburg-western-pomerania-merz-s-cdu-slumps-to-7" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD is leading in polls ahead of regional elections in Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania on September 20, while Chancellor Friedrich Merz's centre-right CDU has fallen to just 7%, according to a new ZDF poll. The result would mark the party's worst-ever showing in a regional election in Germany.</summary></entry><entry><title>Africa: Rethinking the city of tomorrow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70d028a90746b26c2c0bfe5e74ceab5922eea8285ccf8610fb958975398d7722</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T14:24:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-africa-rethinking-the-city-of-tomorrow" /><summary type="html">How should we envision the African city of tomorrow? A city adapted to population growth and climate change, and freed from a colonial past that is still very much present in some places. Africa’s first pan-African architecture biennale, held this week in Kenya, is seeking to answer that question.</summary></entry><entry><title>Senegal: Building a home-grown space industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06fc6b673f0c95dd895b9a736b32d6c6544ebc8ffbf68d7918d588c1920ff400</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T14:22:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-senegal-building-a-home-grown-space-industry" /><summary type="html">Africa’s space ambitions are gathering pace, and Senegal is determined not just to put satellites into orbit, but to build them at home.

Senegalese engineers are already mastering satellite manufacturing in France, with the goal of bringing that expertise back to their country and developing a home-grown space industry.</summary></entry><entry><title>Niger: Kafra oil block could hold 2.5 billion barrels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9b7f354ed34b2c9421e2cdb68f3c066a9dfe2a4648aad2318e3577095a23679</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T14:19:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-niger-kafra-oil-block-could-hold-2-5-billion-barrels" /><summary type="html">Niger’s oil minister held a press conference on Wednesday to address a key issue for the country: the oil reserves Niger could rely on to fuel its development. Most of Niger’s oil production is currently operated by Chinese companies, but one area — the Kafra oil block — could become a cornerstone of economic cooperation with neighbouring Algeria. Active drilling has begun in the block, with the minister announcing that the zone could hold an estimated 2.5 billion barrels of oil. Our correspondent Harold Girard tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo: At least 24 children die in school fire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe707df2112de996eaf5b2245fefca57f83f0582c5ae3224a5108430144b6e9b</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T14:17:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-dr-congo-at-least-24-children-die-in-school-fire" /><summary type="html">At least 24 children have died after a fire broke out at a school in Bukavu, in eastern Democratic Republic of Congo. The blaze reportedly started while children were in class, with some attempting to escape by jumping from higher floors. Adults are also reported to have died, while an investigation into the cause of the fire is underway. Our correspondent Emmet Livingstone tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump begins two-day Ireland visit, security operation costs €20 million</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ed68daa0fcdc4978e7c8f9a08def9a64e1129e62751d87cada6881fb73e2df5</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T14:16:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-trump-begins-two-day-ireland-visit-security-operation-costs-%E2%82%AC20-million" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump arrives in Dublin for a two-day visit to Ireland, where he is expected to meet Irish leaders and spend time at his golf resort in Doonbeg, County Clare. His visit has prompted a major security operation reportedly costing €20 million, while opinions remain divided among locals.</summary></entry><entry><title>BRICS leaders meet in India as wars and US tensions test the bloc</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99e88ce901b5e83397f4559ae0d279436d577da67355566ea1ca372adc2c6c7e</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T10:29:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-brics-leaders-meet-in-india-as-wars-and-us-tensions-test-the-bloc--a8d51de6b163.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-brics-leaders-meet-in-india-as-wars-and-us-tensions-test-the-bloc" /><summary type="html">Leaders of the BRICS nations are meeting in New Delhi on Saturday for a summit focused on trade, investment and global conflicts, as the bloc seeks a bigger role in shaping the global agenda for emerging and developing countries. Our correspondent Navodita Kumari tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis seize key sites around Bab el-Mandeb as Saudi oil exports face disruption</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db09d7402083d4d2ea34a57f4d0313f2b02276bc2281d1a6bd19119f3aa62e13</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T10:27:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-houthis-seize-key-sites-around-bab-el-mandeb-as-saudi-oil-exports-face-disruption--04fa64f2f945.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-houthis-seize-key-sites-around-bab-el-mandeb-as-saudi-oil-exports-face-disruption" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia has stopped transferring oil through a major pipeline after it was attacked by drones.

Meanwhile, Houthi forces have taken control of a strategic port and island in Bab el-Mandeb from Yemeni government forces.

Iran, which backs the rebels, says it had nothing to do with the attacks.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's Putin arrives in India as BRICS leaders begin talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12286214e5a51678ceb01954ed942bca532dcea4fd9baa2a02d20f2dd12222e5</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T10:16:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-russia-s-putin-arrives-in-india-as-brics-leaders-begin-talks--c802e99508f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-russia-s-putin-arrives-in-india-as-brics-leaders-begin-talks" /><summary type="html">President Putin arrived as talks among leaders of the BRICS diplomatic bloc began on Friday in India, amid global geopolitical turmoil, including the war in Ukraine and the conflict in the Middle East.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump will meet with Ireland's leaders before heading to his golf club in Doonbeg</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aba1fa34269f87258fc83b21b90d6b7448a4a1bde6752c695137b16a47c75035</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T10:11:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-trump-will-meet-with-ireland-s-leaders-before-heading-to-his-golf-club-in-doonbeg--4fd079ed115f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-trump-will-meet-with-ireland-s-leaders-before-heading-to-his-golf-club-in-doonbeg" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump arrived Saturday in Dublin, where he'll hold talks with Ireland's president and prime minister, kicking off a weekend visit that's more about a major golf tournament held on a course he owns on the country's Atlantic coast.</summary></entry><entry><title>Céline Dion fever grips Paris ahead of sold-out residency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:407337318226ddf6d24a5a360a83547f54add896b4f57c3cb74118ace982523e</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T10:10:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-c_line-dion-fever-grips-paris-ahead-of-sold-out-residency--1b27a54cd22f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-c%C3%A9line-dion-fever-grips-paris-ahead-of-sold-out-residency" /><summary type="html">It's Céline Dion fever in Paris. She returns to the stage this Saturday, opening a sold-out Paris residency.

It will be the first of 26 concerts over the next eight months. She is making a comeback after a battle with a neurological disorder that has sidelined her career.

On the eve of her first performance, there was a giant free karaoke singalong here in the French capital to get things going.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rennes beat Olympique de Marseille to seize top spot in Ligue 1</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76b1fa2d76d0382ecfa0c1b45e6ba532d65633abdf7c8e12fe31954794ddd427</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T10:09:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260912-rennes-beat-olympique-de-marseille-to-seize-top-spot-in-ligue-1--568e6811f209.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260912-rennes-beat-olympique-de-marseille-to-seize-top-spot-in-ligue-1" /><summary type="html">It’s the same old story for Olympique de Marseille, who have now lost three matches in a row in the French championship. Struggling in every area of the pitch and lacking ideas, the Marseille side have won just one of their last four matches.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Jewish ‘supercop’ runs on Arab ticket in Israeli polls – and sparks a storm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7119e29dd00729bd5ae32cdc486f2859f8444e74f83499822a4e749f5d16fbe</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T09:50:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-jewish-supercop-runs-on-arab-ticket-in-israeli-polls-_-and-sparks-a-storm--26e2eab65f03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-jewish-supercop-runs-on-arab-ticket-in-israeli-polls-%E2%80%93-and-sparks-a-storm" /><summary type="html">Former Israeli police officer Yoav Segalovitz's decision to run as the No. 2 candidate on the Arab Raam party ticket in the October 2026 elections marks a paradigm change in Israeli politics. Far-right politicians have slammed the move, but it could pave the way for an Arab party to join a coalition opposing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his allies.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Swiss researchers use AI to detect early warning signs of natural disasters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2724794db22dc63e6c55ec9f174198848b2416fae700473a8842d1e38e11c156</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T09:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-swiss-researchers-use-ai-to-detect-early-warning-signs-of-natural-disasters--ded7f1a9699b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-swiss-researchers-use-ai-to-detect-early-warning-signs-of-natural-disasters" /><summary type="html">Scientists have long warned of more intense extreme weather events in the decades to come due to our fast-warming climate. The question they are asking is how we are going to be better prepared as we become more prone to natural disasters.A group of researchers in Switzerland believe that artificial intelligence modeling could revolutionise forecasting systems.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kremlin says meeting between Putin and Zelensky at Miami G20 'impossible'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e765c14abbc0aaf838289ef7cb84025aca1f4ee67e5e93f59a8eca7353ab171</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T09:27:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-zelensky-willing-to-meet-putin-at-g20-kremlin-still-to-confirm-attendance" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said he was willing to meet Russian leader Vladimir Putin at the G20 summit in Miami for talks on ending the war. However, the Kremlin immediately ruled it out, saying it was "impossible" and that a meeting would only take place in Russian capital Moscow.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
